<title>FRANCE: Union urges French defence workers to strike.</title>
<headline>Union urges French defence workers to strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>An arm of the Communist led CGT trade union urged workers at France's arsenals and defence firms on Thursday to hold a day-long strike in May to press for wage rises and job security.</p>
<p>&quot;It is urgent to unite people at the local and national levels,&quot; the CGT's FNDT public employee arm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The union urged its members to campaign for higher salary and more job protections via protests and demonstrations throughout the period from April 22 until May 1, paving the way for the day-long strike later in May.</p>
<p>Last October 12, 20,000 defence workers demonstrated in France in favour of jobs protection in their sector. The unions argue that jobs are threatened by military and defence sector reforms planned as part of a transition to an all-volunteer military.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
